{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "274",
   "text": "Why didn't tariffs push up the dollar?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "275",
   "text": "Treasury, the CEA, conventional analysts and markets all expected appreciation. The dollar fell about 10% against the G10.",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "anomaly",
   "toulmin": "unassigned",
   "oper": "unassigned",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#ANOM"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "276",
   "text": "Bessent at roughly 4% appreciation per 10% of tariffs; Miran expecting a rise; Lerner symmetry in the textbooks; going long the dollar as the standard post-election trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "position_map",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#POS"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "277",
   "text": "Lerner symmetry holds — a tax on imports is a tax on exports, even without retaliation",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "278",
   "text": "Tariffs leave capital flows untouched, demand for U.S. assets is constant, and trading partners will not change their own policies",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "279",
   "text": "\"the dollar's downturn was still a bit of a surprise\" — he counts himself among those caught out",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "revised_prior",
   "toulmin": "revision",
   "oper": "revision",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "280",
   "text": "Dollar down ~10% against the G10; a $400-550 imported phone now carries $40-110 of tariff; CNY 7.2, KRW 1400, JPY 140; 55% of China's formal reserves still in dollars",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "281",
   "text": "The Miran paper; IMF working paper on Lerner symmetry; SAFE 2023 annual report; Aitken on the ageing exceptionalism trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "282",
   "text": "Five channels at once — tariffs as fiscal tightening, recession risk hitting equities, China declining to let the yuan slide, Europe's fiscal turn, and a risk premium from treating allies as adversaries",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "283",
   "text": "The dollar was priced for perfection: the flow equilibrium needed ever-larger inflows at ever-higher valuations",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "284",
   "text": "Each of the five channels is plausible and none is decisive on its own",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "285",
   "text": "\"In a sense, the dollar's recent weakness is over-determined\" — he declines to choose",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "286",
   "text": "The consensus he started from — that tariffs mechanically lift the dollar",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "287",
   "text": "The dollar is still strong by most measures; claims about the end of its reign are exaggerated",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "288",
   "text": "The five theories function as rivals to each other, and he keeps all of them live",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#R1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "289",
   "text": "The Taiwan test — how much appreciation will its central bank tolerate, and how would Treasury respond to one-sided intervention? \"This story isn't over.\"",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "deferred_question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_may_5_25#DF"
  },
